{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgw1hhxxss","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"show_dashboard deep-link limit: resourceUri cannot be parameterized without UI-protocol changes","summary":"The show_dashboard MCP tool's meta.ui.resourceUri is a fixed string ('ui://orchestrator/graph') that the MCP app uses as a resource-fetch handle via resources/read. Parameterizing the URI (e.g., 'ui://orchestrator/graph?workspace=...') would require: (1) the MCP client to pass the parameterized URI in its resources/read call, and (2) the resources/read handler to match it. Without those changes the inline widget always shows the daemon-global graph view. Implemented smallest viable version: tool now accepts an optional workspace argument and returns a browser deep_link URL (http://localhost:PORT/graph?workspace=<encoded>) in the result so the user/agent can navigate directly. Session workspace is auto-injected from ctx.workspace (set in mcp-graph.js stdio transport). Back-compat: no workspace arg => original behavior (rendered:true, no deep_link).","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T17:00:26.709Z","vec":[-0.10496562719345093,0.046412259340286255,0.016739988699555397,0.017549974843859673,-0.011463124305009842,-0.05843985825777054,-0.03989885002374649,0.05147331580519676,-0.04990357160568237,0.01156154740601778,-0.03214791789650917,-0.04194054752588272,0.03575165569782257,0.04118211194872856,0.03732810541987419,0.006584043614566326,0.18524861335754395,-0.012614873237907887,0.03309868648648262,-0.017095457762479782,0.07748611271381378,-0.009620011784136295,-0.0020594343077391386,-0.06095866113901138,-0.021027594804763794,-0.061893414705991745,-0.058137014508247375,-0.04607507586479187,0.043281491845846176,0.0286326352506876,0.0249767005443573,0.020138703286647797,-0.16496333479881287,-0.013612223789095879,0.07011710852384567,0.11674270778894424,-0.01632634922862053,-0.0726456344127655,-0.035475969314575195,0.049618352204561234,0.060841117054224014,0.06991159915924072,-0.0162